compact_v5\docs\htmls\V5_DESIGN_OVERVIEW.html:163:      Extended thinking is handled like a signed permission slip. Bedrock may return a thinking block with a signature. On the next turn, v5 may include the previous assistant message again as conversation history, but it must replay only the original signed thinking block. v5 never invents an unsigned thinking block from display text. The UI shows a readable copy for the operator, while the runtime keeps Bedrock's signed block separate.
