compact_v5\docs\htmls\archive\v4_architecture.html:215:    <p class="subtitle">A secure AI coding assistant that runs inside AWS SageMaker notebooks. It reads your code, writes files, edits Jupyter notebooks surgically, creates documents, generates charts, and helps you build software &mdash; all through a chat interface. v4.10.0 shipped 5 Runnable-parity upgrades. v4.10.1 added Context Collapse + Sonnet 4.5 default. v4.10.2 softened the verify-contract. v4.10.3 added ship-gate verifier + cache-boundary regression test + many-skill stress test + clearer permission denials. v4.10.4 closed the largest remaining gap: sub-agents now receive a bounded work-context handoff block (AGENT_STATUS slice + active todos + recent changed files) on top of v4.10.0's env-details. v4.10.5 adopted 3 Learning_Factory prompt-only patterns: post-compact resume protocol, structured summary sections, skill self-patching 4-rule check. v4.10.6 added the html skill: presentation / design / flowchart / architecture HTML deliverables, with screenshot-iteration loop. v4.10.7 hardened destructive-command coverage: ~50 new bash patterns + ~12 python patterns spanning cloud / IaC / orchestration / storage / DB CLI / persistence / system-overwrite, HIGH_RISK_TOOLS excluded from Always-Approve UI, cross-surface mirrored into Claude Code + Learning_Factory hooks. v4.10.8 closed the residual obfuscation escape route (base64/xxd/eval pipe-to-shell now blocked across more interpreters) and hard-blocked recursive folder removal from the agent (`rm -r/-rf/-fr/-R/--recursive`, `rmdir`, `Remove-Item -Recurse`, `shutil.rmtree`, `os.rmdir`, `os.removedirs`, `Path(...).rmdir()`) — single-file cleanup still allowed; the 🧹 Clean button still works in-process. v4.10.9 closed Codex's third local-hook finding by adding a narrow backtick eval+downloader pattern (defense-in-depth only — eval was already excluded from the bash allowlist; zero new false-positive risk). v4.10.10 surfaced the previously-hardcoded `aws_bedrock_only` setting as a UI checkbox in cell 2 of `chat.ipynb` (default ticked = strict). Codex review on v4.10.10: PASS. 134/134 destructive-coverage tests + 122 v4 unit tests + 16/16 hook obfuscation self-test all green.</p>
