compact_v5\docs\htmls\archive\v4_architecture.html:318:            A coding agent automates the developer workflow: read code &rarr; understand intent &rarr; make changes &rarr; verify results. Instead of switching between editor, terminal, and browser manually, you describe the outcome and the agent handles tool orchestration. V3 supports 24 tools covering file operations, code execution, document generation, and codebase intelligence.
compact_v5\docs\htmls\archive\v4_architecture.html:666:            <strong>Data flow (top &rarr; bottom):</strong> User message enters the Agent Loop, which selects tools based on intent. Context Manager tracks token usage and compacts when needed. Tool calls pass through the Security Gate before execution. Bedrock (Claude) handles reasoning and tool selection. Results flow back through the loop until the task is complete.
compact_v5\docs\htmls\archive\v4_architecture.html:876:            Tool selection happens entirely within Claude's reasoning. V3 sends all tool definitions (name + description + JSON schema) with each API call. Claude maps your intent to the appropriate tool and constructs valid arguments. The 5-layer error recovery handles common LLM mistakes (wrong tool name, mismatched types, missing required params) without re-prompting. Lazy loading of doc tools saves ~700 tokens per non-document API call.
